__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.DS_Store
*.swp
praat_prefs/

# Scratch preference directories written by the harnesses. Never read by a
# check -- they exist only so a run cannot inherit, or disturb, the user's
# own Praat preferences. harness/record/roundtrip.sh needs this because
# prefs5 decides the output encoding, and an inherited one made that harness
# pass five times and then fail.
harness/*/prefs/
harness/stress_cases/prefs/

# Probe output written beside a probe when it is run BY HAND. The drivers
# set EML_OUT; the fallback is the current folder, deliberately, so that a
# hand-run can never write into another tree -- but it must not be committed.
harness/disclosure/formpath_*.png
harness/disclosure/worst_*.png
harness/determinism/prefs/
# The parity harness writes a scratch pref dir, same as the others.
harness/parity/prefs/
# The wrapper parse harness writes a scratch pref dir and per-wrapper logs.
# WRAPPERS.tsv is the evidence validate/v35 reads and is NOT ignored.
harness/wrappers/prefs/
harness/wrappers/out/*.log
# The GUI end-to-end harness writes a scratch pref dir and per-run logs.
# DIALOGS.tsv is the evidence validate/v35 reads and is NOT ignored.
harness/gui_e2e/prefs/
harness/gui_e2e/out/*.log
harness/gui_e2e/out/*.png
# The record end-to-end harness writes a scratch pref dir and a driver log.
# RECORD.tsv and the emitted script ARE the evidence and are NOT ignored.
harness/record_e2e/prefs/
harness/record_e2e/out/driver.log
# The form-helper harness plants collision bait -- empty files whose only
# purpose is to already exist when @emlGenerateUniquePath is asked for a
# name. run.sh rebuilds the tree from nothing on every run, because a
# leftover file would change what "already taken" means and quietly move
# every answer. FORMHELPERS.tsv and the driver log ARE the evidence and are
# NOT ignored.
harness/formhelpers/out/scratch/
# The tab-walk probe's raw Praat transcript. TABWALK_JOINED.tsv is the
# evidence validate/v44 reads and is NOT ignored.
harness/tabwalk/out/*.log
# The gui end-to-end run's own HOME. It is pointed inside out/ so a run cannot
# write its figure into the real home directory -- which it did on 13 Aug 2026,
# because @emlSaveConfig had persisted lastPNGFolder there. The figure and CSV
# land in it; ARTEFACTS.tsv records their names and sizes and IS the evidence.
harness/gui_e2e/out/home/

# harness/savepaths: the EVIDENCE is DIALOGS.tsv, ARTEFACTS.tsv, PANEL.png and
# the files each save wrote. Everything below is session state that changes on
# every run and says nothing about the plugin: Praat's own instance lock, the
# scratch pref dir, and the X server and window manager logs. Committing them
# makes every run a diff and buries the four files that matter.
harness/savepaths/prefs/
harness/savepaths/out/work/
harness/gui_adv/prefs/
harness/gui_adv/out/home/
harness/gui_adv/out/xvfb.log
harness/gui_adv/out/wm.log
harness/gui_adv/out/report.utf8.txt
harness/savepaths/out/xvfb.log
harness/savepaths/out/wm.log

# harness/batch: the EVIDENCE is BATCH.tsv, the seven CSVs the batch module
# itself wrote, the seven Info-window transcripts and EXCISED.txt — all of them
# committed, all of them read by validate/v53. out/work/ is not evidence: it is
# the scratch tree the drive builds and destroys on every run — the synthetic
# corpora, the derived headless twin, the per-case include files and the seven
# output folders. It is rebuilt from nothing each time precisely so that a
# leftover corpus or a leftover results CSV cannot change what a run means, and
# committing it would bury the twelve files that do.
harness/batch/prefs/
harness/batch/out/work/

# harness/batchcmd: the EVIDENCE is COMMANDS.tsv, and it is committed. What is
# ignored below is the material the drive builds in order to have something to
# measure -- a folder of synthesised wavs and their TextGrids, the four abort
# probes with their scripts and logs, the scratch CSV, the folder-scaffolding
# probe. All of it is regenerated from scratch by every run and none of it says
# anything about the plugin; committing it would make each run a large diff
# around the one file that matters.
harness/batchcmd/out/fixture/
harness/batchcmd/out/probe/
harness/batchcmd/out/scaffold/
harness/batchcmd/out/probe.csv
harness/batchcmd/out/driver.log

# harness/edittable: the EVIDENCE is EDIT.tsv, DIALOGS.tsv, EXCISED.txt and the
# eleven CSVs the shipped editor itself wrote with their eleven Info-window
# transcripts — all committed, all read by validate/v55. out/work/ is not
# evidence: it is the derived headless twin, the generated dialog tapes, the
# per-case fixtures and the tables each case left behind, rebuilt from nothing
# on every run so that a leftover table cannot change what a case means.
harness/edittable/prefs/
harness/edittable/out/work/

# Two guard harnesses added 15 Aug 2026 keep their evidence and drop their
# scratch: savepaths/guards drives the unwritable-folder and hostile-base-name
# legs (its point is that NO file lands, so it cannot live under out/ where
# v48 asserts of every leg that files did), and newpath drives the
# paired New-after-Draw rebind and the ragged-CSV reader battery.
harness/savepaths/guards_out/work/
harness/newpath/out/work/

# harness/graphaxes (15 Aug 2026): the axis, clip, annotation-panel and stereo
# harnesses behind validate/v62. The EVIDENCE is committed — AXES.tsv,
# STEREO.tsv, BREAKS.tsv, the rendered figures and the screenshot of the
# stereo dialog — because those are what the validator reads and what a
# reviewer needs to see without an X server. What is ignored is scratch: two
# Praat pref dirs (the stereo one is wiped and rebuilt per run so a stale lock
# cannot read as a harness bug), the per-leg Praat logs, and the X server and
# window-manager logs, which are pages of xkbcomp keysym warnings.
harness/graphaxes/prefs/
harness/graphaxes/prefs_stereo/
harness/graphaxes/out/*.log
harness/graphaxes/cases/prefs/

# harness/graphseams (15 Aug 2026): the four legs behind validate/v61 — the
# standalone annotated Kruskal-Wallis draw that used to crash, the wrapper's
# beginner-mode handover, three scatter draws and one export, and a beginner
# save carrying an old advanced session's "Separate figure" choice. The
# EVIDENCE is committed — SEAMS.tsv, the DIALOGS and ARTEFACTS lists, the two
# converted Info reports and the photograph of the advanced scatter dialog —
# because those are what the validator reads and what a reviewer needs without
# an X server. What is ignored is scratch: one Praat pref dir per leg (each is
# wiped and rebuilt per run, so a stale instance lock cannot read as a harness
# bug), the per-leg HOME the save panel writes its figures into, the per-leg
# Praat logs, and the X server and window-manager logs, which are pages of
# xkbcomp keysym warnings.
harness/graphseams/prefs_*/
harness/graphseams/out/home_*/
harness/graphseams/out/*.log
# The adjustment-arm rig's per-arm HOME, ignored on the same rule as the line
# above and for a reason that had to be measured before it was believed. It
# was tracked, and its 13 files are named from the wall clock
# (demo_3groups_Violin_Plot_20260815_175339.png), while adjustarm.sh wipes the
# directory at the top of every run -- so no re-drive could ever reproduce a
# single one of them. redrive_census.sh scored all 13 MISSING on 17 Aug 2026.
# The TSVs, the receipts, the converted reports and the dialog photographs
# beside them are the evidence validate/v61 reads; these were the save panel's
# scratch, kept by accident when the rig was added after the ignore rule above
# was written.
harness/graphseams/adjust_out/home_*/
# The replay leg's own Praat pref dir. Scratch, not evidence.
harness/record/replay_prefs/

# The 15 Aug ruling harnesses. Evidence is tracked; Praat pref dirs, the
# recorder's mid-flight mirror and the per-break-case logs are not -- a break
# log is the transcript of a deliberately broken tree, useful while running and
# noise once the case is recorded in the validator's own count.
harness/drawlayer/out/prefs/
harness/drawlayer/out/*.log
harness/graphseams/*_out/prefs/
harness/graphseams/axis_out/*.log
harness/graphseams/adjust_out/*.log

# harness/axisspec (16 Aug 2026): the one-bin spectrum and the recorded axis,
# behind validate/v67. The EVIDENCE is committed — AXISSPEC.tsv, BREAKS.tsv,
# the rendered figures and the emitted scripts each record leg produced —
# because those are what the validator reads and what a reviewer needs without
# rendering anything. What is ignored is scratch: this rig's Praat pref dir
# (wiped of its lock files per leg, never anybody else's), the per-leg Praat
# logs, the per-break-case v67 transcripts (useful while running and noise
# once the case is in BREAKS.tsv), and the generated replay wrappers, which
# are written fresh on every run and carry absolute paths.
harness/axisspec/out/prefs/
harness/axisspec/out/*.log
harness/axisspec/out/replay_*.praat

# ag2 scratch: form-axis break shadows and probe scratch (Ruling 10b form half, v68)
/tmp/ag2/
harness/formaxis/out/prefs/
harness/formaxis/out/*.code
# The per-break v68 transcripts, one per shadow tree. BREAKS.tsv is the record
# and IS tracked; these are the logs it summarises, rewritten on every run.
harness/formaxis/out/break_*.v68.log

# ag3 scratch: the bracket-caption work (16 Aug ruling, v69). The OCR
# intermediates under harness/bracketcap/out are inputs to tesseract -- the
# cropped caption band and the cropped figure above it, upscaled -- and are
# rewritten by every run of harness/bracketcap/bracketcap.sh. The .ocr and
# .fig.ocr files they PRODUCE are the evidence validate/v69 reads and are
# deliberately not ignored, nor are the PNGs the ruling is proved on.
/tmp/ag3/
harness/bracketcap/prefs/
harness/bracketcap/out/*.band.png
harness/bracketcap/out/*.band.txt
harness/bracketcap/out/*.band.err
harness/bracketcap/out/*.fig.png

# v71 scratch. The sandbox, the break-battery tree copies and the drive output
# all live under /tmp, outside this repository, so nothing here is strictly
# needed -- these two entries exist so that a run redirected into the tree by a
# stray TMPDIR cannot be committed by accident.
ag5_scratch/
v71_work/

# evidence/redrive scratch. run.sh lifts @wizardReportPlan out of
# plugin/scripts/eml-wizard.praat into this file on every run and removes it
# again at the end; a run interrupted between those two points would otherwise
# leave a stale copy of the wizard's procedures in the tree, which is exactly
# the drifting duplicate the extraction exists to avoid.
evidence/redrive/wizard_procs.generated.praat

# batchgui scratch. harness/batchgui/run.sh stages TWO complete plugin trees
# under out/work -- one carrying the shipped setup.praat and one carrying the
# derived copy with the batch registration cut out -- plus a pref dir, a HOME
# and the three-file corpus for each leg. None of it is evidence: the evidence
# is BATCHGUI.tsv, INFO.txt, RESULTS.csv and the five PNGs beside them, which
# are NOT ignored. The trees are rebuilt from nothing on every run, so a
# committed copy would be a second, drifting plugin inside the plugin's own
# repository -- and the one under out/work/prefs_before is a setup.praat with a
# live registration deliberately removed, which is the last file that should
# ever be mistaken for the shipped one.
harness/batchgui/out/work/
/tmp/ag7/

# harness/consumeonce (16 Aug 2026): the consume-once axis publication,
# behind validate/v74. The EVIDENCE is committed — CONSUMEONCE.tsv,
# BREAKS.tsv and the emitted script each record leg produced — because those
# are what the validator reads and what a reviewer needs without running
# Praat. What is ignored is scratch: this rig's own Praat pref dir (only its
# lock files are wiped, per leg, and never anybody else's), the per-leg Praat
# logs, the recorder's crash mirror (a duplicate of the emitted script,
# written row by row so a Table lost to a crash is not lost with it), and the
# per-break-case v74 transcripts, which are useful while a break is being run
# and noise once its line is in BREAKS.tsv.
harness/consumeonce/out/prefs/
harness/consumeonce/out/*.log
harness/consumeonce/out/*/eml_record_mirror.txt
harness/consumeonce/out/break_*.v74.log

# harness/directional (16 Aug 2026): the sign-reversal matrix behind
# validate/v73_directional_p.R. There is no evidence under out/ at all, and
# that is deliberate -- this rig's single artefact is
# evidence/info/v73_directional_info.txt, committed beside the fixture the
# validator reads it against. out/work/ is the staging tree: a copy of the
# driver and a symlink named `plugin` pointing at whichever tree the run was
# asked to exercise, rebuilt from nothing every run so that a symlink left
# behind by a break test cannot make a later run describe a plugin nobody
# selected. Committing it would put a machine-specific symlink and a second
# copy of the driver in the repository. out/driver.log is Praat's echo of the
# capture plus one line; a second copy that can drift from the committed one
# is the thing the capture exists to prevent.
harness/directional/out/work/
harness/directional/out/driver.log

# harness/record's LEGEND leg and its break rig (16 Aug 2026): author ruling B,
# change order 8. The emitted scripts, the figures and REPLAY.tsv are evidence
# and stay tracked. BREAKS.tsv is evidence too -- it is the record of which
# deliberate defect went red and by how much -- but the per-break v75
# transcripts are not: a break log is the transcript of a tree that was broken
# on purpose, useful while it is running and noise once the count is in
# BREAKS.tsv. The shadow trees themselves live outside the repository.
harness/record/replay_out/breaks/break_*.v75.log

# harness/bracketcap's second break rig (16 Aug 2026): author ruling C, change
# order 9, behind validate/v76. BREAKS_V76.tsv is evidence -- it is the record
# of which deliberate defect went red and by how much -- and stays tracked, as
# BREAKS.tsv does for v69. The per-break v76 transcripts are not: a break log
# is the transcript of a tree that was broken on purpose, useful while it is
# running and noise once its count is in the TSV. The shadow trees themselves
# live outside the repository, under the scratch directory the rig names.
harness/bracketcap/out/break_*.v76.log

# The one-line library barrel is GENERATED, at every Praat launch, by
# plugin/setup.praat, into whichever folder the plugin is installed in. On a
# development machine that folder can be this working tree -- harness/walks
# symlinks the repository into a preferences directory -- and the file it
# writes there carries THAT machine geometry in eleven absolute include
# lines. Committing it would put a fourth barrel in scripts/ whose paths are
# right on one machine and wrong everywhere else, beside three shipped ones
# whose paths are relative on purpose. validate/v82 asserts this entry is
# here and that nothing tracked matches it.
plugin/scripts/eml-lib-user.praat
